  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Interface**\n\nI\'ve laid the groundwork. I\'ve chosen a technical dashboard approach as the initial design, and I\'ve integrated key packages like `react-dropzone` and `react-markdown`. I\'m using Tailwind for styling and `clsx` and `tailwind-merge` for utility management. My focus now is on defining the user experience flow for essay structuring.\n\n\n**Implementing the AI**\n\nI\'m focused on integrating the AI service first. I\'ve defined the component structure: Sidebar, EssayQuestion, PlanningStructure, Sources, ConclusionFrame, and EssayPlanPreview. I\'ve chosen `Inter` and `Libre Baskerville` for typography. The color palette will be earth tones. I\'ll utilize `motion` for transitions and I\'ll revisit installing any more packages.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now build the **IBDP Geography Essay Architect**. \n\nI\'ve selected a **\"Modern Academic\"** aesthetic: combining clean, technical data grids (for structure) with warm, earthy tones like sage, cream, and charcoal to reflect the geographic theme.\n\n### \360\237\217\227\357\270\217 UI Architecture\n- **Stage Navigation**: A progress tracking sidebar to move between Question, Planning, Evidence, and Synthesis.\n- **Dynamic Input Modules**: Areas for Paragraph Focuses and Concepts that allow students to add and remove items dynamically.\n- **Structural Frameworks**: A toggle for PEEL vs. PEECAL, with descriptions of each to guide the student.\n- **AI Synthesis**: A refined prompt that takes all student inputs\342\200\224including extracted text from sources\342\200\224to generate a structured plan.\n\nI\'ll start by creating the utility functions, the Gemini service, and then the main application structure.\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 269471698
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
