    modified_response: "The **IBDP Geography Essay Architect** is now ready for your class. This app acts as a digital faculty member, helping you structure complex geographic arguments while keeping your own intellect and planning at the center of the process.\n\n### \360\237\214\237 Key Features:\n*   **Targeted Mark Schemes**: Tailors the depth and complexity of the plan specifically for **10, 12, or 16-mark** questions.\n*   **Academic Frameworks**: Choose between **PEEL** (Point, Evidence, Explain, Link) or **PEECAL** (adds Counter-argument and Analysis), ensuring you meet top-band evaluation criteria.\n*   **Case Study Evidence & Uploads**: Supports **PDFs, PPTs, Word docs**, and **Web Links**. The AI reads these sources to help you integrate specific, real-world case study data.\n*   **Intellectual Scaffolding**: Requires you to manually input paragraph focuses and core geographic concepts (e.g., *Scale*, *Sustainability*) before generating a response.\n*   **Concluding Directives**: Set the exact \"direction of travel\" for your conclusion to ensure a consistent, unified argument.\n\n### \360\237\232\200 How to use:\n1.  **Question Analysis**: Enter your essay prompt and define the key terms you\'ll use in the intro.\n2.  **Manual Planning**: Define the sub-themes for your body paragraphs and select your chosen academic framework.\n3.  **Source Integration**: Upload your lesson notes or case study docs.\n4.  **Synthesize**: Generate a comprehensive, structural roadmap that tells you *how* to write the essay, rather than doing it for you.\n\nYou can now start planning your next Geography internal assessment or exam practice essay!"
