  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I\'ve built the **IBDP Geography Essay Architect** (GeoStrategy), a structured tool designed to help you plan high-mark responses (10, 12, or 16 marks) using professional geographic frameworks.\n\n### Key Features:\n- **Sequential Planning Flow**: Guides you through Question Analysis, Manual Planning, Evidence Gathering, and Conclusion Strategy.\n- **Geographic Pillars**: Explicitly select from the **4Ps** (Place, Process, Power, Possibilities) and **2Ss** (Scale, Spatial Interaction) to ensure your analysis meets IB criteria.\n- **Flexible Frameworks**: Choose between **PEEL** (Point, Evidence, Explain, Link) or the more evaluative **PEECAL** (Point, Evidence, Explain, Counter-Argument, Analysis, Link) \342\200\224 the latter being ideal for top-tier 16-mark responses.\n- **Source Integration**: Upload PDF, Docx, or PPT files, or add web links to ground your plan in real-world case studies and lesson notes.\n- **AI-Powered Synthesis**: Using **Gemini 1.5 Pro**, the app synthesizes your manual inputs and sources into a formal essay roadmap without writing the essay for you, preserving your intellectual ownership.\n- **Geometric Balance Design**: A bold, neubrutalist \"GeoStrategy\" aesthetic featuring thick borders, geometric shadows, and a clean slate/emerald color palette for an academic studio feel.\n\n### How to use:\n1. **Define the Question**: Enter your prompt and select the mark value.\n2. **Plan the Argument**: Identify your paragraph focuses and select your conceptual pillars (4Ps/2Ss).\n3. **Gather Evidence**: Upload your case study materials.\n4. **Set your Stance**: Prompt the AI with how you want the evaluation to land.\n5. **Architect**: Click \"Synthesize\" to generate your printable roadmap.\n\nYour application is ready to use in the preview!"
