  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Concluding the Development**\n\nI\'ve successfully wrapped up the development. Now, I\'ll provide a concise summary of the work accomplished and offer the user testing URLs. I focused on creating an IBDP Geography essay planning interface, structured around mark schemes, definitions and more. This multi-step process is ready for user input and testing.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The **GeoStrategy IBDP Geography Essay Architect** is now fully built and ready for testing. \n\nYou can access your live application using the **Shared App URL** provided in the sidebar (or top of this chat). Since the app is already running in your AI Studio environment, there is no extra \"hosting\" step required\342\200\224it is active and accessible now.\n\n### **Features Integrated:**\n*   **Structured Question Analysis:** Select between 10, 12, or 16-mark thresholds to adjust the depth of the AI\'s guidance.\n*   **Manual Planning Core:** Specialized inputs for defining key terms and mapping out body paragraphs, ensuring student intellect drives the argument.\n*   **Geographic Pillars (4Ps & 2Ss):** Toggle buttons for Place, Process, Power, Possibilities, Scale, and Spatial Interaction to ground the essay in the IB framework.\n*   **Framework Selection:** Toggle between **PEEL** (Point, Evidence, Explanation, Link) and **PEECAL** (Point, Evidence, Explanation, Counter-Argument, Analysis, Link) for higher-level evaluative responses.\n*   **Evidence Vault:** A drag-and-drop area to upload case study PDFs, lesson notes (images/docs), or PPTs which the AI will analyze to extract specific evidence.\n*   **Conclusion Strategizer:** A dedicated section to set your terminal stance (e.g., \"agree to a large extent\").\n*   **Geometric Balance Design:** A clean, high-contrast academic aesthetic with a \"Neubrutalist\" feel, prioritizing readability and structure.\n\n### **How to test it:**\n1.  Open the **Shared App URL**.\n2.  Input a past paper question (e.g., a 16-mark \"Examine...\" question).\n3.  Upload a case study PDF or some screenshot notes in the \"Sources\" step.\n4.  Select **PEECAL** for the 16-mark structure.\n5.  Click **\"Synthesize Outline\"** to see your structured roadmap.\n\n**Note:** Ensure you have your `GEMINI_API_KEY` configured in the **Secrets** panel for the essay synthesis to function."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 731978230
