  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Key Configurations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the practical implications of the \"pro\" subscription. Specifically, I\'m examining the code related to the `GEMINI_API_KEY` to understand how the API key is handled. I\'m noting that `vite.config.ts` plays a crucial role in defining this environmental variable. This should help clarify the hosting setup for our expert user!\n\n\n**Analyzing Key Usage**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the code related to the Gemini API key. The `.env.example` file highlights the expected format, while `src/lib/gemini.ts` shows how it\'s used. The AI Studio environment automatically injects the key from user secrets, clarifying they can use their own key through the AI Studio UI if they want to. I\'m noting the distinction between a Gemini Advanced subscription and the AI Studio\'s API access, including free tiers and billing options. This system provides a Dev and Shared URL, indicating the \"hosted\" status of the app.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "To use your Gemini API key and get the app fully functional, follow these steps:\n\n### 1. Where to put your API Key\nIn Google AI Studio, you don\'t need to paste the key directly into the code. Instead:\n1. Look at the left-hand sidebar in the AI Studio interface.\n2. Click on the **Secrets (key icon)** tab.\n3. Add a new secret:\n   - **Name:** `GEMINI_API_KEY`\n   - **Value:** Paste your API key from the [Google AI Studio API Key manager](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey).\n4. The app will automatically detect this and use it to power the \"Synthesize Outline\" button.\n\n### 2. Using your \"Pro\" Subscription\nIf you have a **Gemini Advanced** subscription (the $20/month plan for personal use), it\'s important to note that the **Gemini API** used for building apps is slightly different:\n*   **The API has its own Free Tier:** You likely won\'t need to pay anything to use this app. Google provides a very generous free tier for the Gemini 1.5 Pro model in AI Studio.\n*   **Capacity:** If you find you are hitting \"Quota Exceeded\" limits frequently, you can enable billing in your Google Cloud Project, but for an individual student/teacher use case, the Free Tier is usually more than enough.\n\n### 3. Hosting & Testing\nYour app is **already hosted**! You can see the links in the panel above:\n*   **Development App URL:** Use this while you are making changes.\n*   **Shared App URL:** Use this once you are happy with it. You can send this link to your phone, tablet, or students. It works just like a real website.\n\n### Summary of what we built:\n*   **Geometric Balance Theme:** A high-contrast, \"Neo-Brutalist\" academic design with bold borders and emerald accents.\n*   **4Ps & 2Ss Integration:** You can now toggle Place, Process, Power, Possibilities, Scale, and Spatial Interaction to guide the AI.\n*   **Multi-Step Planning:** Forces \"student intellect\" by requiring paragraph focuses and concepts before generating the AI roadmap.\n*   **PEEL/PEECAL Support:** Structured specifically for IB assessment criteria.\n\n**Would you like me to add a feature to export the finished plan as a PDF or text file?**"
