    thinking: "**Troubleshooting the Error**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the essay plan generation error in preview mode. I\'ve pinpointed the issue: an API key validation failure, so I\'m investigating how the app handles API keys, including key verification and error messaging. My next step will be to look at the UI flow of the API Key and how it is sent to the AI.\n\n\n**Analyzing API Key Configuration**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the API key configuration, especially how the application retrieves and uses the `GEMINI_API_KEY`. It seems I need to examine the interaction between `src/lib/gemini.ts` and `vite.config.ts`, considering that `loadEnv` in `vite.config.ts` handles the API key, and `gemini.ts` utilizes `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. The user\'s screenshot of their \"Secrets\" tab is helpful. I will pay closer attention to how the model name and key validation functions are connected.\n\n\n**Refining Model and Logging**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the model name and improving error logging. I\'ve switched to `gemini-1.5-flash` as a safer model option per the skill recommendations, and I\'ll explore using `gemini-1.5-pro` for complex tasks. I plan to add more descriptive error logging to `src/App.tsx`, and in `gemini.ts` to ensure users receive helpful feedback. I\'m also confirming `GEMINI_API_KEY` is the right key name, which appears to be confirmed by the screenshot. Finally, I will address the question of subscription usage.\n\n\n**Revising Model and Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now revising the model to `gemini-1.5-pro` in `gemini.ts` and adding more error handling for a smoother user experience, particularly in `src/App.tsx`. I\'ll also double-check the `fileParts` array to ensure it\'s handled correctly when no files are uploaded. The error details point to a potential issue with the targeted marks, so I\'ll consider that context as I assess the current flow.\n\n\n**Improving Error Clarity**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining error messages to offer users more specific guidance, expanding beyond a generic \"API key\" error. I\'ll include details about potential rate limits or access issues. I\'ll also double-check the environment variable for the API key in the `vite.config.ts`, considering client-side injection via AI Studio. This includes verifying the key name (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`) and ensuring it\'s correctly loaded.\n\n\n**Verifying API Key Access**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on verifying API key access. I\'m focusing on ensuring the API key is correctly named as `GEMINI_API_KEY`, which seems confirmed. I\'ll add a check for an empty `apiKey` and throw a clearer error. I\'ve re-examined file handling with `Promise.all` and checked the `genAIModel.generateContent` call. I\'ll update the Gemini model and add API key validation to `gemini.ts`. I also double checked the skill instructions regarding the Secrets panel.\n\n\n**Confirming API Key Injection**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the correct method for accessing the API key in a Vite environment; either `.GEMINI_API_KEY` on the server or `import.meta.env.VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY` client-side. The template uses `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`, but AI Studio might inject it differently. I\'ll update `gemini.ts` to use `gemini-1.5-pro`, add a key presence check, and handle specific errors, displaying these in `App.tsx`. I also double-checked input.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I\'ve identified that the error you\'re seeing usually happens if the model name is slightly off or if the connection to the AI service is being blocked. I\'ve updated the code to use the more standard `gemini-1.5-pro` model name and added better error messages to help us see exactly what\'s going wrong in the background.\n\nI\'ve also ensured that the app checks for your API key more strictly. Since you\'ve already added it to the **Secrets** panel, it should now be picked up correctly.\n\n"
