    thinking: "**Refining the Logic**\n\nI\'ve significantly hardened the application logic and implemented comprehensive fallbacks. My latest task involves verifying that `import.meta.env` in the Vite configuration correctly handles environment variables from the deployment platform. It\'s a key area to test before proceeding.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The `API_KEY_MISSING` error typically occurs when the environment variables aren\'t correctly passed from the platform to the application\'s client-side code. I have implemented a more robust detection and fallback system to ensure your key is recognized.\n\n### Changes made:\n1.  **Updated `vite.config.ts`**: Improved the way environment variables are captured. It now explicitly pulls from the platform\'s secrets (`process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`) and injects them into the application bundle.\n2.  **Enhanced `src/lib/gemini.ts`**: Added a fallback check for both `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` and `VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY`. It also now uses lazy initialization to ensure the key is only checked at the moment you try to generate a plan.\n3.  **Refined Error Handling**: Updated the UI to provide clearer instructions if the key is still not detected after these changes.\n\n**Important Next Steps:**\n1.  **Refresh your browser tab** where the app is running (this ensures you are using the latest version of the code).\n2.  **Verify the Secret Name**: In the **Secrets** panel (top-right menu), ensure the name is exactly `GEMINI_API_KEY`.\n3.  If it still fails, you can try adding a second secret named `VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY` with the same value, as some environments prefer that prefix for client-side visibility.\n\nThe server has been restarted to apply these new configurations. Please try generating a plan again!"
